    "nonlinear_virial_collapse_and_halo_transition": {
      "comparison_with_superfluid_dark_matter_berezhiani_khoury_2015": "While superfluid dark matter (Berezhiani & Khoury 2015) postulates a new dark boson species (m ~ eV) that clusters as pressureless dust on linear scales and condenses into a P(X) ~ X^{3/2} phonon superfluid inside cold galaxy halos (requiring a thermal phase transition at T = T_c that breaks down in hot galaxy clusters), TEP posits zero dark-matter particles (omega_cdm = 0). Both the linear clustering multiplier M_s = 1 + y_s/sqrt(2) = 6.26 (omega_phi = 0.11816) and the screened halo/cluster profiles arise from the single universal proper-time field phi with P_{,X} = k sqrt(xi) + 2 xi sourced purely by ordinary baryons (omega_b), smoothly connecting linear BAO/CMB scales to galaxy and rich-cluster mass profiles without a thermal condensate breakdown or collisionless NFW cusp.",
